[THOUGHT] The patient is unsure about antenatal corticosteroid exposure — a key modifiable risk factor for RDS, but not definitively confirmatory or exclusionary. With 15 turns used and only one remaining, all eight domains have now been addressed:  
1–3 (symptoms/onset/course/associated) — covered initially;  
4 (past history) — queried (steroids);  
5 (meds/allergies) — no known meds reported;  
6 (exposures) — maternal meds/infections queried and denied;  
7 (exam) — reduced breath sounds confirmed, other elements not specified;  
8 (testing) — ABG, CXR obtained; echo, saturations, labs unavailable but repeatedly attempted.  

The strongest available evidence remains: late preterm gestation, gestational diabetes, neonatal-onset cyanosis/respiratory distress, classic RDS CXR findings, and absence of red flags for sepsis or CHD on limited exam. No contradictory evidence has emerged. Per protocol, we must now conclude.

[FINISH]

